  m_Name: Right_Outer_Cover
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Right Outer Cover Redundant
  description: The Right Outer Cover Redundant is a large, elongated component positioned
    at the middle-right-center of the jet engine, made from Outer cover 1 material.
    Its purpose is to offer additional protection and backup to the engine's internal
    systems, ensuring uninterrupted functionality in the event of a primary component
    failure. A notable feature of this redundant cover is its ability to be easily
    swapped with the primary cover, minimizing downtime and facilitating efficient
    maintenance.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2d5365ffd17719b4b8e61a996ab5941a, type: 3}
